===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|nl|dum|cnôop}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|*knōp}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*knaupaz}}, one of several ''kn-'' words related to {{m|gem-pro|*knuttô|t=knot}}. Cognate with {{cog|de|Knauf}}.

====Noun====
{{nl-noun|m|-en|knoopje}}

# [[button]] (knob or small disc serving as a fastener)
# [[knot]] (i.e. a [[loop]] of string or any other long flexible material which cannot be untied without pulling part of the string through the loops)
#: {{usex|nl|Ik zit in de knoop.|I'm in a hard spot. / I'm all tied up.}}
# {{lb|nl|mathematics}} [[knot]]
# {{lb|nl|nautical}} [[knot]] (i.e. a unit of [[velocity]], corresponding to traveling a distance of 1 [[nautical mile]] per [[hour]])
# {{lb|nl|botany}} [[node]], [[joint]]

